content.text:
Here’s what was going wrong.

**Cause:** In `globals.css`, rules for `html[data-public-layout]` were **always** resetting `--sidebar` and `--card` on the footer and traject action bar to **light** neutrals (`neutral-white` / `neutral-100`), with an explicit comment that they should stay light **regardless of theme**. That hid dark-mode tokens from `themes/default.css` (`.dark`), so the footer and the `from-card` scroll gradient stayed light while `main` followed dark mode.

**Change:** Those overrides now apply only when the document is **not** in dark mode, using `:not(.dark)` so they still apply for light (and for `html` without a mode class). With `html.dark`, footer and traject bar inherit the normal semantic `--sidebar` / `--card` values.

```193:211:/Users/psoudan/workspace/05-Procertus/Procertus-ui-experiment/packages/ui/src/styles/globals.css
  /*
   * Public registry/onboarding (light appearance): footer + traject sticky bar use a
   * crisp neutral strip. Under `html.dark`, semantic `--sidebar` / `--card` apply instead.
   */
  html[data-public-layout]:not(.dark) [data-slot="footer"] {
    --sidebar: var(--neutral-white);
    --sidebar-foreground: var(--neutral-950);
    --sidebar-accent-foreground: var(--brand-primary-700);
    --card: var(--neutral-white);
    --card-foreground: var(--neutral-950);
  }
  html[data-public-layout]:not(.dark) [data-slot="traject-action-bar"] {
    --card: var(--neutral-100);
    --card-foreground: var(--foreground);
  }
```

No updates were required in `footer.tsx` or `public-registry-app-shell.tsx`; they already use `bg-sidebar` / `bg-card`, which now follow the theme once the variable overrides are gated.

